## prodshare_n128_233_x3_final.mpmct1 (2026-07-24, from the server ~/tds/prodshare233)
Second production circuit through the PRODUCT-SHARE nonlinear encoding, using
the EFFICIENCY+HARDENING revision (commits 2b16aa70 encoding pass; d32bedf7
docs; see docs/PRODUCT_SHARE_UPDATE.{tex,pdf} and
docs/NONLINEAR_GADGETIZATION.{tex,pdf}). Three changes vs the [2,2,3,3]
circuit above: the [2,3,3] plan (one deg-2 base + two deg-3 tower terms --
25% fewer gates at identical measured security), a NONLINEAR CASCADED band
fill (products over data wires AND earlier band wires, so the band is no
longer a set of learnable affine invariants of the whole circuit), a mirror
fill F' after the output bookend, and randomized fold-fragment emission order.
Pipeline:
  fresh C (128w x 3000 g57, SECRET, server-side only; gen_sandwich_gadget
  seed 1) -> sliced_sandwich_cnot (m_C=m_D=3000, s=896) = 7920 g / 256w ->
  product-share gadgetize (PROD_K=1 PROD_DEG=2 PROD_K_HI=2 PROD_DEG_HI=3
  PROD_FILL_NL=2 => plan [2,3,3], band 56): 281068 g / 568 w, endpoint verify
  PASSED (low-256 == sandwich, 200 samples) ->
  fmix (FROZEN_DB_DIR=frozen_m1_m11, guards deg9/span30/terms 1024:2048):
  - PHASE A (generation-100 dose over the DB-ELIGIBLE material, seed 41):
